    "title": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "7 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-03 23:23:00 CDT Expires: 2025-09-04 00:00:00 CDT Urgency: Immediate Severity: Severe Certainty: Observed Instruction: For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a building. Target Area: Maries, MO; Miller, MO SVRSGF\nThe National Weather Service in Springfield has issued a\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for... West central Maries County in central Missouri... Northeastern Miller County in central Missouri...\n* Until midnight CDT.\n* At 1123 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Eldon, moving southeast at 45 mph.\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n* Locations impacted include... Eldon, Iberia, St. Elizabeth, Tuscumbia, and Marys Home.",
